The preview container auto-start was demo-user-only, and the iframe could load before the Theia HTTP server was ready — causing an intermittent redirect to `https://anybot.brainswarmrobotics.com/theia/` (no port), which matches no nginx route.

## Backend — `theia_service.py`

- **`is_theia_ready(port)`**: TCP socket probe (1 s timeout) that returns `True` only when the Theia HTTP server is actually accepting connections, not just when Docker reports the container as running.
- **`ready` field** added to every `_get_single_container_status` result, surfaced as `preview_ready` / `booking_ready` in `get_container_status` and flowing through to the `/theia/status` response.

## Frontend — `TheiaIDE.jsx`

- **Readiness gate on iframe**: `isRunning` now requires both `containerRunning` (Docker state) **and** `containerReady` (`preview_ready` / `booking_ready`). The iframe is withheld until the HTTP server is confirmed up, eliminating the broken-redirect race.

- **Universal polling**: The 5-second re-poll loop previously ran only for demo users. It now runs for **all users** whenever the active container is not running or not yet ready, and also tracks booking container readiness when the user has an active booking.

```js
// Before — polling gated behind demo-user check
if (user?.isDemoUser || user?.isDemoAdmin || user?.isDemoMode) { … }

// After — polls for everyone until both containers are ready
const previewNotReady = theiaStatus.preview_status !== "running" || !theiaStatus.preview_ready;
const bookingNotReady = theiaStatus?.has_active_booking && (
  theiaStatus.booking_status !== "running" || !theiaStatus.booking_ready
);
if (!previewNotReady && !bookingNotReady) return; // stop polling
```

