## Auth Middleware + RBAC — Slim 4 Middleware Stack (DOC-03)

### Context
ZYNC ERP now has:
- ✅ Slim 4 + PHP-DI foundation (PR #21)
- ✅ Core database tables: `roles`, `departments`, `users`, `permissions`, `role_permissions`, `user_sessions`, `audit_log` (PR #22)
- ✅ 7 system roles seeded (VD, CEO, Chef, Teamchef, Arbetsledare, Arbetare, Läsbehörighet)
- ✅ Memory bank with all project rules (PR #20)

The next step is to build the **middleware stack** defined in DOC-03. This is the security backbone of the entire system.

### CRITICAL: Read the memory bank first
Before making ANY changes, read these files thoroughly:
- `.github/copilot-instructions.md` — Complete technical requirements
- `CLAUDE.md` — Project context and architecture decisions

### What this PR creates

#### 1. Middleware classes in `zync-erp/app/Middleware/`

Create the following Slim 4 PSR-15 middleware classes. Each must implement `Psr\Http\Server\MiddlewareInterface`:

##### `AuthMiddleware.php` (DOC-03 §3.4)
Verifies that the user is authenticated via session (for web UI) or JWT (for API).

```php
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Middleware;

use Psr\Http\Message\ResponseInterface;
use Psr\Http\Message\ServerRequestInterface;
use Psr\Http\Server\MiddlewareInterface;
use Psr\Http\Server\RequestHandlerInterface;
use App\Core\Auth;

class AuthMiddleware implements MiddlewareInterface
{
    public function process(ServerRequestInterface $request, RequestHandlerInterface $handler): ResponseInterface
    {
        // Check session-based auth first (web UI)
        if (Auth::check()) {
            // User is authenticated via session, inject user data into request
            $user = Auth::user();
            $request = $request->withAttribute('user', $user);
            $request = $request->withAttribute('user_id', $user['id'] ?? null);
            return $handler->handle($request);
        }

        // TODO: Check JWT token in Authorization header (for API routes, future PR)
        // $token = $this->extractBearerToken($request);
        // if ($token) { ... verify JWT ... }

        // Not authenticated — redirect to login (web) or return 401 (API)
        $path = $request->getUri()->getPath();
        if (str_starts_with($path, '/api/')) {
            $response = new \Slim\Psr7\Response();
            $response->getBody()->write(json_encode([
                'success' => false,
                'error' => [
                    'code' => 'UNAUTHORIZED',
                    'message' => 'Autentisering krävs'
                ]
            ]));
            return $response
                ->withHeader('Content-Type', 'application/json')
                ->withStatus(401);
        }

        // Web UI: redirect to login
        $response = new \Slim\Psr7\Response();
        return $response
            ->withHeader('Location', '/login')
            ->withStatus(302);
    }
}
```

